  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The methodology is presented only as a proof-of-concept simulation, and the abstract does not validate the model against real-world outbreak data from an active camp.",
      "what": "This study presents a methodology to evaluate how different refugee and internally displaced person camp layouts influence human movement and disease transmission. The approach is demonstrated through proof-of-concept experiments using the JUNE agent-based epidemic model to simulate interaction patterns and disease spread within camp boundaries.",
      "why": "It establishes a framework for camp planners to use spatial design and layout configuration as active tools for mitigating epidemic outbreaks in highly vulnerable settlements."
    }
